{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string: str, character: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove first and last occurrence of specified character from string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to process\n        character (str): The character to remove\n\n    Returns:\n        str: Modified string with first and last occurrences removed\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(character)\n\n    # If the character is not found, return the original string\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(character)\n\n    # If first and last occurrences are at the same position, there's only one occurrence\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:]\n    else:\n        # Remove both the first and last occurrences\n        # Construct the new string by skipping characters at first_idx and last_idx\n        result_chars = []\n        for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n            if i != first_idx and i != last_idx:\n                result_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
