{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(items: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    Returns None if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        return None\n\n    frequency_map = {}\n    for item in items:\n        frequency_map[item] = frequency_map.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    max_count = -1\n    max_item = None\n\n    # Iterate through the frequency map to find the item with the highest count.\n    # In case of ties, the item that appears first in the dictionary's iteration order is returned.\n    for item, count in frequency_map.items():\n        if count > max_count:\n            max_count = count\n            max_item = item\n\n    return max_item"}
