{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a positive integer can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This is true if and only if its binary representation contains no consecutive 1s.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Negative numbers or zero cannot be represented as sum of non-zero powers of 2\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for consecutive 1s in the binary representation\n    # Example: 10 (decimal) is 1010 (binary). No consecutive 1s.\n    # Example: 6 (decimal) is 110 (binary). Has consecutive 1s.\n    while number > 0:\n        if (number & 1) == 1 and ((number >> 1) & 1) == 1:\n            return False\n        number >>= 1\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array of integers.\"\"\"\n\n    def _count_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            if x == 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _count_non_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for x in arr:\n            if x != 0:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _calculate_ratio(zeroes: int, non_zeroes: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Performs floating-point division to compute the ratio.\"\"\"\n        return float(zeroes) / non_zeroes\n\n    num_zeros = _count_zeros(array)\n    num_non_zeros = _count_non_zeros(array)\n\n    return _calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)"}
