{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Helper function to reverse elements from index 0 to i in the given list.\n    def flip(arr, i):\n        start = 0\n        while start < i:\n            arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            i -= 1\n\n    # Helper function to find the index of the maximum element in arr[0...n-1].\n    def find_max_index(arr, n):\n        max_val = arr[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for k in range(1, n):\n            if arr[k] > max_val:\n                max_val = arr[k]\n                max_idx = k\n        return max_idx\n\n    # Create a copy of the input list to sort, as per design context.\n    arr_copy = list(arr)\n    n = len(arr_copy)\n\n    # The main pancake sort algorithm: repeatedly find the max and flip it into place.\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted portion.\n        max_idx = find_max_index(arr_copy, curr_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct final position.\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # If the max element is not at the front, flip to bring it to index 0.\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                flip(arr_copy, max_idx)\n            # Flip the entire current unsorted portion to move the max element to its sorted position.\n            flip(arr_copy, curr_size - 1)\n\n    return arr_copy"}
