{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_idx = find_first_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False # Element not found in the array\n\n    last_idx = find_last_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # Calculate the count of occurrences\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2\n    return count > n / 2"}
