{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union, Tuple\n\ndef convert(z: Union[complex, float, int]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Convert complex number to polar coordinates.\n\n    Args:\n        z: Complex number or real number to convert.\n\n    Returns:\n        Tuple of (magnitude, angle_in_radians).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(z, complex):\n        z = complex(z)\n    \n    magnitude = math.sqrt(z.real**2 + z.imag**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n    \n    return magnitude, angle"}
