{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses a helper function to check for primality.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative number.\")\n\n    def _is_prime(n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n        Returns True if n is prime, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
