{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    The digit '0' is a special case and its frequency does not cause invalidation.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(integer)\n    digit_counts = Counter(s)\n\n    for char_digit, count in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_value = int(char_digit)\n\n        # As per design, the digit '0' can appear any number of times and does not\n        # invalidate the number based on its frequency vs. its value.\n        if digit_value == 0:\n            continue\n\n        if count > digit_value:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
