{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "import math\n\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of the first n bits\n    equals the sum of the last n bits using combinatorial mathematics.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    # The count is the sum of (C(n, k))^2 for k from 0 to n.\n    # C(n, k) represents the number of ways to choose k ones out of n bits.\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        combinations_k = math.comb(n, k)\n        total_count += combinations_k * combinations_k\n    return float(total_count)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "def large_product(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], k: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists,\n    selecting one factor from each list.\n    \"\"\"\n    products = []\n    # Generate all possible products from list1 and list2\n    for x in list1:\n        for y in list2:\n            products.append(x * y)\n\n    # Sort the products in descending order\n    products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the top k largest products\n    return products[:k]"}
