{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo_cache = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum using the recursive equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Results are memoized to optimize performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n\n    if n in _memo_cache:\n        return _memo_cache[n]\n\n    # Recursively calculate the sum of f(n/k) for k = 2, 3, 4, 5 using integer division\n    sum_of_divisions = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    # The maximum sum is either the sum of its divisions or n itself\n    result = max(sum_of_divisions, n)\n\n    # Store the computed result in the cache before returning\n    _memo_cache[n] = result\n\n    return result"}
