{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeated character in a given string.\n    Returns None if no unique character is found or the string is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    # Count character occurrences in the string using a dictionary.\n    char_counts = {}\n    for char in input_string:\n        char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n    # Iterate through the string again to find the first character with a count of 1.\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n\n    # If the loop completes, no non-repeating character was found.\n    return None"}
