{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def _generate_gap_sequence(n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a decreasing sequence of gaps for Shell Sort.\n    Starts with n // 2 and halves the gap until it's 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    gaps = []\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        gaps.append(gap)\n        gap //= 2\n    return gaps\n\ndef _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr: list, gap: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an insertion sort on elements separated by a given gap.\n    Modifies the array in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(gap, n):\n        temp = arr[i]\n        j = i\n        # Shift elements greater than temp to the right\n        while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n            arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n            j -= gap\n        arr[j] = temp\n\ndef shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original input.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a copy of the input array to avoid modifying the original\n    arr_copy = list(arr)\n    n = len(arr_copy)\n\n    # Handle edge cases for empty or single-element arrays\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr_copy\n\n    # Generate the gap sequence (e.g., [n//2, n//4, ..., 1])\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    # Apply insertion sort for each gap in the sequence\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr_copy, gap)\n\n    return arr_copy"}
