{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    Handles positive, negative numbers, and zeros efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = float('-inf')  # Tracks the global maximum product found.\n    max_ending_here = 1         # Tracks the max product of subarray ending at current position.\n    min_ending_here = 1         # Tracks the min product of subarray ending at current position, crucial for negative numbers.\n\n    for num in arr:\n        if num == 0:\n            # If zero is encountered, any subarray including it will have product 0.\n            # Reset products to 1 to start a new subarray product calculation.\n            max_ending_here = 1\n            min_ending_here = 1\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, 0) # Zero itself is a possible maximum product.\n        else:\n            # A negative number can turn a small min product into a large max product.\n            # Store current max_ending_here before it's updated for min_ending_here's calculation.\n            temp_max = max_ending_here\n            max_ending_here = max(num, num * max_ending_here, num * min_ending_here)\n            min_ending_here = min(num, num * temp_max, num * min_ending_here)\n\n            # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n    \n    return int(max_so_far)"}
