{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "def max_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an increasing subsequence of the array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    dp = list(arr)  # dp[i] stores the maximum product of an increasing subsequence ending at index i\n\n    max_overall_product = max(dp) # Initialize with the maximum single element product\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                # If arr[i] can extend the increasing subsequence ending at arr[j]\n                # Update dp[i] if a larger product is found\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n        # Update the overall maximum product after computing dp[i]\n        max_overall_product = max(max_overall_product, dp[i])\n\n    return max_overall_product"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def normalize_tuple(t):\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a sorted, normalized form for order-independent comparison.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(t))\n\ndef find_intersections(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Finds intersecting tuples between two lists, using order-independent comparison.\"\"\"\n    intersection_set = set()\n    for t1 in list1:\n        normalized_t1 = normalize_tuple(t1)\n        for t2 in list2:\n            normalized_t2 = normalize_tuple(t2)\n            if normalized_t1 == normalized_t2:\n                intersection_set.add(t1)\n                break\n    return intersection_set\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\n    Compares tuples (a, b) and (b, a) as equivalent.\n    \"\"\"\n    return find_intersections(list1, list2)"}
