{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def _is_sorted(lst: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list is sorted in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    return all(lst[i] <= lst[i+1] for i in range(len(lst) - 1))\n\ndef _validate_inputs(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates input constraints, raising ValueError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n    if not (len(list1) == size and len(list2) == size):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both lists must be of the specified size.\")\n    if not _is_sorted(list1):\n        raise ValueError(\"First list must be sorted.\")\n    if not _is_sorted(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Second list must be sorted.\")\n    if size == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Size cannot be zero for median calculation.\")\n\ndef _find_median_binary_search(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Implements efficient median finding using a binary search approach.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure list1 is the shorter array for binary search optimization,\n    # though here both lists are of equal size 'n'.\n    n = size\n\n    # Binary search for the partition point 'i' in list1.\n    # 'i' represents the number of elements taken from list1 for the left half.\n    # 'j' (n - i) represents the number of elements taken from list2 for the left half.\n    low = 0\n    high = n # i can range from 0 to n\n\n    while low <= high:\n        i = (low + high) // 2\n        j = n - i\n\n        # Define boundary elements for the partitions\n        # max_left_X is the largest element in the left partition of listX\n        # min_right_X is the smallest element in the right partition of listX\n        max_left_1 = list1[i - 1] if i > 0 else -float('inf')\n        min_right_1 = list1[i] if i < n else float('inf')\n\n        max_left_2 = list2[j - 1] if j > 0 else -float('inf')\n        min_right_2 = list2[j] if j < n else float('inf')\n\n        # Check if the partition is correct:\n        # max element of left half <= min element of right half (across both lists)\n        if max_left_1 <= min_right_2 and max_left_2 <= min_right_1:\n            # Correct partition found. The median is the average of the two middle elements.\n            return (max(max_left_1, max_left_2) + min(min_right_1, min_right_2)) / 2.0\n        elif max_left_1 > min_right_2:\n            # i (elements from list1) is too large; reduce i\n            high = i - 1\n        else: # max_left_2 > min_right_1\n            # j (elements from list2) is too large; increase i\n            low = i + 1\n    \n    # This part should ideally not be reached if inputs are valid and size > 0\n    return -1.0 # Or raise an error indicating an unexpected state\n\ndef get_median(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    Assumes lists are sorted and of equal size as specified by 'size'.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(list1, list2, size)\n    return _find_median_binary_search(list1, list2, size)"}
