{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert tuple to dictionary by pairing adjacent elements.\n\n    Raises ValueError if input tuple has an odd number of elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_tuple) % 2 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuple must have an even number of elements to form key-value pairs.\")\n\n    result_dict = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple), 2):\n        key = input_tuple[i]\n        value = input_tuple[i+1]\n        result_dict[key] = value\n    return result_dict"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions.\n    Handles empty lists and rotations greater than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate effective rotation to handle positions > n\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: the end part to move to the front, and the remaining start part\n    # The split point is n - effective_positions\n    split_point = n - effective_positions\n    \n    # Extract the elements that will move to the beginning\n    end_slice = input_list[split_point:]\n    \n    # Extract the remaining elements that will follow\n    start_slice = input_list[:split_point]\n    \n    # Concatenate the slices to form the rotated list\n    return end_slice + start_slice"}
