{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer to the left by d positions.\n    The most significant bits wrap around to the least significant positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    NUMBER_OF_BITS = 32\n    # Normalize the rotation count to be within the range [0, NUMBER_OF_BITS-1]\n    # A negative d would result in a right shift modulo NUMBER_OF_BITS.\n    # For example, -1 % 32 = 31, which is equivalent to a left shift of 31 or right shift of 1.\n    normalized_d = d % NUMBER_OF_BITS\n\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # Part 1: Bits shifted left, potentially exceeding NUMBER_OF_BITS\n    left_shifted_part = number << normalized_d\n    # Part 2: Bits that wrapped around from the left\n    wrapped_around_part = number >> (NUMBER_OF_BITS - normalized_d)\n\n    # Combine the two parts and mask to ensure the result is 32-bit\n    result = (left_shifted_part | wrapped_around_part) & ((1 << NUMBER_OF_BITS) - 1)\n    return result"}
